cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Metriplectic Completion of the Frohmanian Symplectic Tether: Thermodynamic Structure and Lean Formalization for the Navier–Stokes Equations (abstract algebraic formalization and companion paper)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Frohman
    given-names: Benjamin Stanley
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7068-3718"
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Texas, United States
    email: frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenFrohman/frohmanian-metriplectic-ns"
keywords:
  - metriplectic
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Frohmanian Symplectic Tether
  - Lean 4
  - abstract algebra
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for an abstract algebraic metriplectic formalization
  in Lean 4, together with a working paper. The Lean development checks
  energy conservation and nonnegative entropy production for an abstract
  metriplectic system, and the purely algebraic obstruction that a
  symmetric bracket degenerate on the Hamiltonian also vanishes when the
  Hamiltonian is placed in the first slot. It is not a Clay Millennium
  Problem proof. The Navier–Stokes specialization in the Lean file is a
  placeholder. Kernel checks are not PDE or physical proofs. Recovery of
  the continuum Navier–Stokes–Fourier equations is not formalized.
